# BUG REPRO: #8944 over-drop on http1 — head-gap check with a later BARE < rule.
#
# The http request tx is first presented to detection at progress 0 (request_started)
# and completes in a single packet (tx_progress 5). The head candidate (accept:flow
# request_complete, hook 5) has a head-of-list gap (5 > detect_progress_orig 0).
#
# The later accept:flow http1:<request_complete rule legitimately covers the gap
# (bare rule, no keyword — it matches at completion). Correct behaviour: the request
# is accepted (no default app policy drop).
#
# main: no coverage suppression -> "missing fw rules at list start" -> default app
#   policy drop (over-drop, #8944 family).
# bug-8944-new/v3: max_in_progress_lte_hook is computed from stored rule state; the
#   < rule has never been inspected (its hook 5 is beyond the current progress), so it
#   has no stored state and does not count -> same over-drop.
# the #8944 fix (firewall-bug-8944-new/v5): max_in_progress_lte_hook is computed from
#   the final candidate list (this-pass prefilter candidates count) -> suppresses the
#   gap -> accept (correct).
accept:hook tcp:all any any <> any any (flow:not_established; sid:1021;)
accept:hook tcp:all any any <> any any (flow:established; sid:1022;)
accept:flow http1:request_complete any any -> any any (sid:852;)
accept:flow http1:<request_complete any any -> any any (sid:853;)
